  "title": "Pin risk: how a defined-risk spread becomes undefined over a weekend",
  "summary": "Example: a short $100/$105 call spread with the stock at $99.97 late on expiration Friday. It looks like a full win. But holders can exercise until about 5:30 pm Eastern after an after-hours rally. You can then be short the stock all weekend. Close any spread with pin risk before the close.",
